WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.880
As I told you guys some time ago, I requested
an absentee ballot in the city of Boston.

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:12.530
I requested one for the September 1st primary
and I requested one for the November 3rd general

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:13.530
election.

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:19.530
And in fact, both my girlfriend and I sent
our applications on the same day two weeks

00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:21.789
ago to the city of Boston.

00:00:21.789 --> 00:00:27.999
What was really weird was that within five
days she had her absentee ballot already back

00:00:27.999 --> 00:00:32.320
and was able to fill it out for the September
1st primary.

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:35.960
And I figured, oh, I'm guessing mine will
get here the next day.

00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:36.960
And it didn't.

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:39.579
Well, it's probably just one more day.

00:00:39.579 --> 00:00:45.489
Maybe I missed the day's mail with my ballot
and it's going to be delivered to me tomorrow.

00:00:45.489 --> 00:00:46.489
Boston's really small.

00:00:46.489 --> 00:00:49.850
You know, three miles gets you almost anywhere
in the city proper.

00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:50.850
No big deal.

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:53.050
Can't imagine it would be much of a delay.

00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:57.239
Well, my absentee ballot didn't come in for
another day or two.

00:00:57.239 --> 00:01:00.840
I was away all of last week in the bunker,
as many of you remember.

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:05.840
I figured my ballot will definitely be waiting
for me by the time I get back.

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:06.840
Right.

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:07.840
Got back yesterday.

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:09.200
Still not here.

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:10.680
Started to find it strange.

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:14.010
Now we're only 13 days from the actual primary.

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:15.600
My girlfriend got hers in five days.

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:16.600
She's already sent it in.

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:18.350
Where's my ballot?

00:01:18.350 --> 00:01:23.560
I call the city of Boston, city of Boston,
Elections Department explains.

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:27.020
And they say, oh, yeah, we got yours today.

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:28.750
Meaning yesterday, right?

00:01:28.750 --> 00:01:30.980
August 17th.

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:33.720
But I sent it on August 2nd.

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:36.000
That's fifteen days.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:38.490
And my girlfriend sent hers on the same day.

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:44.830
How did my ballot end up delayed two weeks
when we sent our applications out on the same

00:01:44.830 --> 00:01:45.830
day.

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:52.130
And the woman at Boston elections says it's
because here we go now it's because of what's

00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:54.800
going on with the post office.

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:57.140
Two items.

00:01:57.140 --> 00:02:00.140
Letters with a single, you know, just a singles.

00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:01.140
Didn't have to stamp it.

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:06.790
But, you know, just a standard letter, not
a package sent on the same day could be delivered

00:02:06.790 --> 00:02:09.250
more than 10 days apart.

00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:11.959
Now, much the same way.

00:02:11.959 --> 00:02:17.740
If I get the ballot today or tomorrow and
send it, could it again be delayed 14 days?

00:02:17.740 --> 00:02:19.349
Is that conceivable?

00:02:19.349 --> 00:02:22.569
If so, that will be after the September 1st
primary.

00:02:22.569 --> 00:02:23.689
Will it still be counted?

00:02:23.689 --> 00:02:25.799
It's certainly supposed to be counted.

00:02:25.799 --> 00:02:31.709
But if the city of Boston assumes ballots
won't take more than two days here in Boston

00:02:31.709 --> 00:02:37.280
because, again, it's a three mile wide city
and then 40 days go by after the primary,

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:38.810
maybe they say, let's stop counting now.

00:02:38.810 --> 00:02:40.890
I can't imagine any more ballots are coming
in.

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:43.400
So this is truly a mess.

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:49.629
And remember, this is all by design, limiting
overtime hours so that even though my application

00:02:49.629 --> 00:02:55.680
and my girlfriend's application probably arrived
to be sorted on the same day, if you prevent

00:02:55.680 --> 00:03:00.060
overtime, you prevent sorting, which prevents
the ballot from being handed to the carrier,

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:01.459
which delays delivery.

00:03:01.459 --> 00:03:03.950
And in this case, it delays processing.

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:04.950
This is no joke.

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:09.180
And if this is happening in Massachusetts,
just imagine what is going on in places with

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:13.349
inferior social services and inferior infrastructure
in general.

00:03:13.349 --> 00:03:19.200
So needless to say, my plan is to drive my
ballot to city hall in the next few days,

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:20.909
assuming it comes in today or tomorrow.

00:03:20.909 --> 00:03:25.870
Now, will this lead to protests because they
actually seemed warranted?

00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:33.599
This is a major direct attack on the democratic
systems we thought we had at their core.

00:03:33.599 --> 00:03:37.579
People e-mailing me saying, you know, David,
I looked at my ballot.

00:03:37.579 --> 00:03:41.180
The online system says my ballot was sent
10 days ago.

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:42.379
Haven't received it.

00:03:42.379 --> 00:03:43.950
My town's even smaller than Boston.

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:45.670
It's two miles wide or whatever.

00:03:45.670 --> 00:03:52.209
I hate to say it, but to have more certainty
that your vote will be counted.

00:03:52.209 --> 00:03:58.040
You might have to vote in person and given
the pandemic, that's horrible and everybody

00:03:58.040 --> 00:04:00.209
needs to figure out what's best for them.

00:04:00.209 --> 00:04:02.669
What level of risk are you willing to tolerate?

00:04:02.669 --> 00:04:06.040
I wish I had better news, but I don't.

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:07.040
But I don't.

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:15.779
We're going to have more coverage of this
on our

00:04:15.779 --> 00:04:21.639
Instagram page.

